.TH NDP-RESPONDER-LITE 8 "October 2026" "ndp-responder-lite 0.1.0"
.SH NAME
ndp-responder-lite \- Linux static IPv6 neighbor discovery responder
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ndp-responder-lite
.RB [ \-c " config.toml" ]
.RB [ \-\-check ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
ndp-responder-lite answers IPv6 Neighbor Solicitations for configured prefixes.
It runs on specified Ethernet interfaces, replying to both
Duplicate Address Detection (DAD) and unicast neighbor resolution.
.PP
The daemon requires Linux, Ethernet interfaces, and CAP_NET_RAW capabilities.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " PATH"
Path to TOML configuration file. Default: /etc/ndp-responder-lite.toml.
.TP
.B \-\-check
Validate configuration syntax and semantics, then exit without opening sockets.
.TP
.B \-\-help
Print command-line help.
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print version information.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/ndp-responder-lite.toml
Default configuration file.
.TP
.I /usr/share/ndp-responder-lite/example.toml
Example configuration file provided by the package.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RUST_LOG
Tracing log filter. Default: info.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ip (8),
.BR systemctl (1)
